{
  "title": "koylu_muhabbet_sorhan",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "node:start",
      "type": "START",
      "position": "(0.0, 0.0)"
    },
    {
      "id": "node:selam",
      "type": "DIALOGUE",
      "position": "(350.0, 0.0)",
      "character": "Sorhan",
      "text": "Blessings upon you, gatekeeper. The steppe wind blows through the manes of our horses. I groom the colts in the stable; what do you inquire?"
    },
    {
      "id": "node:opt_normal",
      "type": "DIALOGUE_OPTION",
      "position": "(700.0, -180.0)",
      "character": "Gatekeeper",
      "text": "Sorhan, how fare the village mounts and pack beasts?"
    },
    {
      "id": "node:opt_kriz",
      "type": "DIALOGUE_OPTION",
      "position": "(700.0, 0.0)",
      "character": "Gatekeeper",
      "text": "If enemy cavalry approaches from the plain, are our horses swift enough for flight or maneuver?"
    },
    {
      "id": "node:opt_karar",
      "type": "DIALOGUE_OPTION",
      "position": "(700.0, 180.0)",
      "character": "Gatekeeper",
      "text": "What say you regarding the itinerant farrier who arrived yesterday?"
    },
    {
      "id": "node:rep_normal",
      "type": "DIALOGUE",
      "position": "(1050.0, -180.0)",
      "character": "Sorhan",
      "text": "Horses listen not to grievances, but to the heart, gatekeeper. I trimmed the hooves of our two black war horses and fed them steppe grass. The village cavalry can fly like the wind whenever duty summons."
    },
    {
      "id": "node:rep_kriz",
      "type": "DIALOGUE",
      "position": "(1050.0, 0.0)",
      "character": "Sorhan",
      "text": "A Kipchak mount never tires, master. If cavalry advances, we flank them from the rear and lay an ambush in the gorge. A warrior who masters his mount is worth ten infantrymen on the field of honor."
    },
    {
      "id": "node:rep_karar",
      "type": "DIALOGUE",
      "position": "(1050.0, 180.0)",
      "character": "Sorhan",
      "text": "The farrier with the nail in his heel came to the stables. He explained how outlaws deliberately hobbled mounts on the pass; I inspected the shoes, and he was truthful. He forged crescent shoes for all our stallions; our beasts will stumble no more."
    },
    {
      "id": "node:act_normal",
      "type": "ACTION",
      "position": "(1400.0, -180.0)",
      "description": "Köy Morali",
      "action_type": "SCRIPT",
      "action_script_ref": "res://src/diyalog/actions/koy_moral_action.gd",
      "values": [
        "2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "node:act_kriz",
      "type": "ACTION",
      "position": "(1400.0, 0.0)",
      "description": "Köy Morali",
      "action_type": "SCRIPT",
